codex
Implemented a native Track B generator based on equation (1.7) of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.02296).

Local results:

- 34,353,664-candidate shipping language; 0/200,000 random guesses.
- Four adversarial attacks each succeeded 0/8 times.
- Reference scan: 1,687,770 mean operations; compact gcd route: at most 76 operations.
- All G1–G9(c) local gates pass.
- Four-atom, 21-character answer.

Deliverables:

- [gen_2203_02296.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2203.02296/gen_2203_02296.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2203.02296/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2203.02296/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2203.02296/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2203.02296/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2203.02296/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The sole blocker is STEP 4: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” before inference for every arm, leaving zero scored oracle attempts. The error transcripts are preserved honestly; the family cannot yet be declared hardened or submitted. No `REJECTED.md` was written because this is an infrastructure/quota failure, not a G/H/V failure.
